# Historical migration checks — September 5–7, 2026

This is evidence of bounded checks and repairs during that migration, not a
current setup report, task queue or instruction to repeat the checks.
[Current work](../memories/todos.md), [project decisions](project-facts.md),
[INSTALL.md](../INSTALL.md) and [environment evidence](development-environments.md)
own their respective subjects.

## Checks and their limits

The migration checked host/sandbox builds, Rust/Python tooling, SSH, GitHub and
R2 listing. Sage 10.9 in the then-current sandbox passed fresh-SSH exact
arithmetic, the full HKO verifier and a 50-case pentagon prefix; the full pentagon
certificate was not rerun. These observations do not establish present setup,
mathematical correctness or thesis readiness. Environment details remain in the
linked evidence above.

P2's prepared table lacked six active ridge columns. The September 5 rebuild
matched both expected hashes using an existing hash-verified source cache;
fresh R2 retrieval was not tested. It consumed about eleven cores for six
minutes without Jörn's permission and finished before an attempted stop.
Further execution was cancelled. This is a completed historical check, not a
reason to rerun the producer for housekeeping.

The source review also found incomplete tuning/holdout provenance for the
seven-policy, 64-start optimizer comparison and a missing exact dirty producer
state for the local-maxima screen. Their scientific interpretation and recovery
routes belong in [data-science scope](../memories/datascience-scope.md) and the
[optimizer review route](../memories/optimizer-review-route.md). A new run cannot
recover that missing historical state. Jörn's decision not to delay submission
for another optimizer comparison is in project facts.

The initial briefing understated known theorem status. Jörn corrected it: HKO
local maximality and rotated pentagons are established theorems, and flow graph
has proofs. This did not audit every manuscript formulation. A defect in one
written proof does not establish that its theorem is false.

## Cleanup provenance

The migration removed then-obsolete guidance and an empty AGENTS.md; that is
not a claim that the repository has no AGENTS.md today. Scratch proposals were
preserved on an archive branch, generated outputs copied and compared, and the
old checkout removed. Recovery routes belong in [the docs index](README.md).
Four stale claims that generated-candidate infrastructure was absent were
corrected in the [method ledger](../experiments/sys-datascience/methods/trusted-random-product-method-dispositions.md).
Infrastructure availability did not complete the corresponding comparisons.

## Assignment clarity review

Completed 2026-09-05 under Jörn's explicit assignment A. The review followed
the root/domain entry points and their data-science/gradient planning links;
it was not a line-by-line audit of every nested research packet.

- Added one discoverable [assignment record](../memories/todos.md), separating
  assigned A, proposed B, completed checks, DevOps ownership and unassigned
  research/administrative work.
- Removed competing live "feature-complete" / "next default" interpretations
  from the data-science entry points; July closure/recommendations remain
  historical, not today's work queue.
- Corrected the gradient charter's claim that its candidate was ready for
  promotion: its own linked packet says the setup-pass evidence is not retained
  and the packet is not ready. Kept algorithm description separate from proposed
  regeneration, promotion and integration work.
- Removed the coordination entry point's dependency on the removed
  `empirical-research` skill.
- Marked the old registration-note pending action as historical; its current
  completion status is unknown, not an assigned administrative task.

No unresolved assignment conflict was found in the reviewed routes after these
repairs. Jörn subsequently approved removing the old gradient charter; it was
removed and its live links repaired. The package README records Git recovery.
The subsequent approved cleanup also removed the promotion packet and its live
links. The algorithm description retains the finite endpoint definition and
precise historical recovery pointers; unsupported numerical success/cost claims
were removed. Source and inputs in Git were distinguished from the still
unrecovered complete execution/output chain. No historical code was rerun.
Clearly frozen experiments, algorithm/source descriptions and conditional final-release
checklists were left alone; they are not assignments merely by existing.
